 "verdict": "consistent once read from the cipher: 76 signs = 76 letters (with two composite signs), 20 groups = 20 words; one letter per shape except the 4-flag (ف x4 and ث in مكلثم); the text as enciphered has يعض (record بعض), مشفق (record مشفو) and يمص (record مص); و two shapes (2-hook, box), as the compiler says",
 "notes": "Rows 3-8 of image 0084_0132: 16 + 13 + 15 + 12 + 16 + 4 = 76 by eye (record 77 = 16,13,16,12,16,4). Plain 1.3x zooms of each half line, 2-2.5x on the look-alikes. Two composite signs are counted once each: the small circle joined by a stroke to a 4-flag (O4, the ح of لحاجة; neither \"ي\" nor \"ف\" fits there, the record counted it as two signs) and the pair of uprights at the head of طعنت (Dh, ط; neither upright occurs alone in the chain). Counted as separate parts the chain has 78 signs and each of the two words one surplus sign. Keyed as enciphered: the small circle is ي in يدفع, so the first words of the parallel half-lines are يعض and يمص (فاذا طعنت يعض عضه مشفق / واذا سللت يمص مصه مرضع), not بعض and مص (ب is the V-on-a-bar of كالقعب, كب); مشفو ends in the ف-shaped sweep, which is ق in كالقعب, so it is مشفق. The waw in two forms (2-hook in ولها, box in واذا) is the encipherer's slip the compiler notes on 64r l.9."
